some things are best kept contained  after all this is the founding principle  behind the scp foundation themselves to  secure and contain the most dangerous  anomalies in order to protect human  lives but within the foundation itself  are things which should never be  uncovered secrets that must never be  told secured behind multiple layers of  containment like the seven seals of  revelation is a threat so high level in  its nature that it can't even be given a  class scp-5999  but in order to truly understand this  late series scp we have to go all the  way back to one of the earliest anyone  looking for scp-001 will quickly realize  that there are several different  entities and anomalies that share this  designation many reasons have been given  for this classification quirk perhaps  they were all discovered in the early  days of the foundation before the  current numbering system was introduced  others have suggested that many  different  scp-001s are an intentional misdirection  by the foundation to keep the nature of  the true first scp a closely guarded  secret one of the many entities and the  one we'll be referring to as scp-001 to  understand  scp-5999 is otherwise known as the  database information about the databases  kept a secret to the entire scp  foundation apart from the overseer  council the reason behind this well that  would be because this scp-001  contains details of the very nature of  the foundation itself including its  creation not how the organization was  founded mind you how it was created and  by whom we're about to break the most  powerful layer of containment of all the  fourth wall you see to you or i the scp  foundation and its vast catalog of user  generated articles on the creative and  the creepy are nothing more than a  source of entertainment it can be fun to  study the lore and the nuances of  different scps appreciating the  imagination and hard work that the  authors put into writing them it can  even inspire us fuel our own written  endeavors whether that takes the form of  fan fiction independent stories original  scps or even a youtube series but when  all is said and done we all know that  the scp foundation is fictional and they  know it too pieced together from various  fragments of information within their  own archives the database contains  everything the foundation knows about  the real world authors of the scp wiki  just like we told you it's time to weigh  a fond farewell to the fourth wall the  metaphorical barrier that separates what  we know to be real from what we know to  be purely fiction the fact that they  exist in this fictional capacity is  something the overseer council hopes to  hide from the rest of the foundation's  personnel but they also have plans in  mind for the scp wiki writers  responsible for creating them and  expanding the roster of anomalies they  keep contain the scp wiki entry on  scp-001 the database closes with a  proposal a plan from the o5 council to  reach the wiki's authors in the real  world through memetic kill agents that  will put them to sleep and then kill  them with that important background  context in mind now let's go all the way  back to the other end of the scp wiki  and take a look at scp-5999  when first accessing the file you the  reader will notice a few format  differences between this entry and  others within the scp archive each  section of  scp-5999 is hidden behind an encryption  and accessing these will reveal the  different levels of this entry remember  how we mentioned the seven seals of  revelation at the start of this video  that wasn't a coincidence in the bible's  book of revelation there are seven  symbolic seals securing a book that john  of patamos saw in his vision of the  apocalypse when these seven seals are  broken and the book is opened this  symbolizes the second coming of the  messiah and marks the beginning of the  biblical apocalypse in much the same  vein scp-5999  is sealed in seven different parts each  behind its own encryption culminating in  one apocalyptic ending so at this point  you're probably thinking what actually  is  scp-5999 what could be so dangerous that  it has to stay hidden in multiple  segments  well on the surface  scp-5999 is just a story it details one  of the scp foundation's many  investigations into an anomalous object  nothing too strange about that but  there's something more to it since with  the foundation there always is and it  has something to do with the images at  the header of each section of the entity  at the top of each part of scp-5999  is a picture of a group of candles seven  to be exact but the further down you  read one by one the candles start to go  out until you reach the end of scp-5999  delving into the first of these sections  the  entry describes a corpse that seems to  be cursed with multiple anomalous  properties after the assault and murder  of one miss jacqueline hallcroft her  remains were scattered according to this  entry any person coming into contact  with a part of miss holcroft's deceased  body or anyone who learns about what  caused her death will experience  anomalous effects these manifest in  various ways for example subjects may  hallucinate that they see a disheveled  woman with wounds similar to miss  holcroft's before her dismemberment this  site is sometimes accompanied by sounds  of whispering and even begging that  calls the subject seeing and hearing  things by their name others have  reported hearing an unknown song set to  the tune of twinkle twinkle little star  the anomalous influence of miss  holcroft's dismembered remains is known  to continue until a subject's death with  many reporting seeing the woman's  deceased body lurking in their old  photos or suffering sleep paralysis as  they feel something being forcibly  removed from their guts some subjects  even report discovering body parts and  organs anything from fingers to eyes to  teeth to hair and finding it at random  places such as when opening a drawer or  in their food finally a number of  subjects affected by the remains of miss  holcroft have reported a specific  irrational fear the fear that the chains  are weakening even after the foundation  recovered jacqueline holcroft's bones  and her remains were buried in a proper  funeral the effects that her dead body  parts had over living subjects did not  stop subjects reported their children  went missing and the attendees at miss  holcroft's funeral were somehow  spontaneously disemboweled after the  ceremony to keep these effects to a  minimum the foundation apparently has a  containment procedure in place the  scp-5999 entry details something called  procedure seven-fold wherein the scp  foundation gathers seven civilians and  brings them to a location called  albright manor on october 30th these  seven people are sedated and awake on  the night of october 31st all entrances  to albright manor are sealed trapping  the civilians inside observe via network  of surveillance devices throughout the  manner procedure seven fold always  results in the deaths of the seven  civilian witnesses brought in by the  foundation whether they are told to  perform a ritual or offered as a  sacrifice is unclear the following  morning foundation cleanup crews will  remove the remains of these people  disposing of their bodies with an  incinerator for the rest of the year  until procedure sevenfold needs to be  conducted again foundation personnel on  site at albright manor are instructed to  be careful around any surfaces that  contain the phrase  this is where i died by now you are most  likely wondering what the remains of  miss holcroft and procedure sevenfold  have to do with anything we've talked  about so far what is the connection to  scp-001 the database is there something  linking an anomalous corpse with the  foundation's knowledge of its own  fictional existence what does a fear of  the chain's weakening mean and why do  none of these questions seem to  acknowledge what those seven candles  represent or why they're still gradually  going out scrolling further through  scp-5999 doesn't seem to yield many more  answers though in fact the more of the  sections you look into the less it seems  to be about miss holcroft or even make  any link to the database and the deeper  you go the fewer candles remain lit the  next few portions of the  scp-5999 entry are dedicated to  completely different investigations that  have little to nothing to do with  procedure sevenfold ms holcroft's corpse  and the anomalous effects it creates are  also absent in later segments of this  entry in the scp archive so if the  cursed body parts of jacqueline holcroft  are not  scp-5999 then what is one report details  the fates of a mobile task force trapped  in a fog shrouded town here they  encounter a lamb that appears to be  undead and evolves into an ungodly  winged beast before the mtf team's very  eyes another that follows is a  transcript of an exorcism during a  classified foundation operation  one agent grace was possessed by a  demonic entity and sent to the  department of demonology specialist in  demonic psychology dr peter mcneal  attempted to remove the demon inhabiting  agent grace however after trying to  intimidate the demonic entity with  various passages from biblical texts it  appears as though maybe the demon was  able to spread its influence to both  agent grace and dr mcneil of course  neither of these reports seemed to  answer any of the pressing questions or  explain the exact nature of scp-5999  as you go further into the entry you  can't help but notice how often chains  are referenced in fact that seems to be  the only thing constant in all these  disjointed segments mentions of a  failure of the chains to hold what lies  beneath and chains that have become too  few in number to hold it all create the  sense that something once was locked up  sealed securely away is managing to  break free then finally as the last  candle goes out you are literally  brought face to face with the horror of  scp-5999 and its true nature is revealed  to you a decaying desiccated corpse  stares out of the screen at you its eyes  are sunken deep into its skull lips  shriveled almost completely away  exposing rows of rotten teeth could it  be miss holcroft's body you aren't sure  what you are sure of is the corpse's  face is getting closer to the screen and  now it's smiling at you you can feel  your heart pounding beating against your  rib cage as the world around you begins  to fade and your life slips away from  you the last thing you see is the grim  face of the corpse staring out at you  with its dead sunken eyes the truth of  scp-5999 is that it has been  specifically designed to kill whoever  reads it by whom you may be asking by  the scp foundation themselves cast your  mind back to the database and remember  that the overseer council are aware of  their own fictional existence they know  that they aren't real and plan to use  him a meta kill agent to take out the  scp wiki authors that created them  scp-5999 is that kill agent an entity  created by fiction to kill those living  in reality  scp-5999 works by drawing a person in  offering disjointed and disconnected  horror stories as a means of grabbing a  reader's attention further and further  down through the entry that person will  go searching for the meaning behind  these chilling tails and therein lies  the trap each layer each section of  scp-5999 that you read is another candle  extinguished and with every flame that  goes out a seal is broken a chain  becomes unbound allowing the entity  contained within the archive and tree  itself to get closer its sole purpose is  to fulfill the proposal laid out by the  o5 council after learning that they were  fictional along with the entire scp  universe by pulling you in with the  mystery and intrigue of the confusing  convoluted stories  scp-5999 is able to deploy jumping out  of the screen towards you condemning you  to a dark and grisly fate or maybe  that's just what the o5 council and the  scp foundation wants us to think either  way it might just be safer to get your  scp knowledge here at scp explained and  speaking of go check out  scp-1730 what happened to site 13 the  full story compilation and  scp-5545 mysterious tunnels in  antarctica abnormality for more  terrifying tales but at least these ones  won't kill you probably

